{"ts":"2026-08-24T10:06:40.662Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"365e646596cb83e6152b34c6","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"files_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files/2","value":{"path":"scripts/verify-release-changelog-date.sh","scope":"project","note":"executable proof for the release workflow invocations, which the package.json changelog check never reaches"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-24T10:06:40.662Z"}],"before_hash":"d7080add2f06d0bdc6ca6764aab12e8b89fba57a188e9258377c220e69c0732a","after_hash":"f3a19e5f2ac20004a13a9e031ee4166dbcef12ff173e0c347ab46042a7ea0f0e","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-08-24T10:06:41.071Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"365e646596cb83e6152b34c6","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-24T10:06:41.071Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"CodeRabbit was right that the linked test only covered the package.json invocation and never reached the direct pm-changelog commands in the release workflow. Added an executable check that does both halves. The static half enumerates every tracked file containing a generator invocation and asserts each file's flagged count is not below its site count, which fails when any single site loses the flag; verified by removing the flag from one of two release.yml sites and watching it report one of two and exit non-zero. The behavioural half runs the generator twice on the same probe version 2026.1.2, deliberately chosen so its calendar date cannot coincide with today, and asserts the heading is 2026.1.2 - 2026-01-02 with the flag and 2026.1.2 - 2026-08-24 without it, so the test states the defect rather than merely asserting the fix."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-24T10:06:41.071Z"}],"before_hash":"f3a19e5f2ac20004a13a9e031ee4166dbcef12ff173e0c347ab46042a7ea0f0e","after_hash":"822c20b7481ff7cb0e690793994e6604f8a0ed883aa808aeecca7eedfc7832f5","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-08-26T18:42:02.455Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"2f9c6839329462b65cdd5d36","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-26T18:42:02.455Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Release workflow fix: replaced the two hand-rolled node dist/cli.js invocations in the \"Build and generate changelog\" step of .github/workflows/release.yml with 'npm run changelog:full' and 'npm run changelog:check'. The hand-rolled calls passed --version but omitted --date-from-version, --respect-item-release and the unbounded --output-budget/--output-limit args that changelog:full carries, so the release commit wrote a clock-dated CHANGELOG.md while npm run changelog:check (CI, release:check) regenerated with --date-from-version and could then fail on a later unrelated commit on main. The \"Update release version\" step already runs npm version before this step, so --release-version-from-package in the scripts resolves to the release being cut. --github-step-summary was dropped because changelog:full has no such flag; reintroducing it would mean a third hand-rolled invocation and the drift it caused. Also aligned the RELEASE_NOTES.md generator invocation (~line 697) with release:notes in package.json by adding --respect-item-release and the unbounded --output-budget/--output-limit args it was missing. Extended scripts/verify-release-changelog-date.sh with a section that fails if any direct node dist/cli.js block in release.yml omits --date-from-version, and confirms the step delegates to the npm scripts; verified non-vacuous by reverting the workflow fix (exit 1) and restoring it (exit 0)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-26T18:42:02.455Z"}],"before_hash":"822c20b7481ff7cb0e690793994e6604f8a0ed883aa808aeecca7eedfc7832f5","after_hash":"259f6eb50fbf1bdc30872f1521d7c8567e31bb962113a4735679e5a39d45a442","item_hash_version":2}
{"ts":"2026-08-26T18:42:06.810Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"2f9c6839329462b65cdd5d36","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-26T18:42:06.809Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Generate-vs-check drift class: when a release workflow hand-rolls a generator invocation separate from the package.json scripts that CI and release:check use, the two diverge silently. The workflow commits a CHANGELOG.md generated with one flag set (e.g. the UTC clock date fallback) while changelog:check regenerates with another (--date-from-version), and a later changelog:check on main fails on a commit that never touched the changelog. The remedy is to never hand-roll the invocation in the workflow: delegate to the same npm script for both generation and check, so there is exactly one source of truth for the flag set. A regression test must key on the direct node dist/cli.js call sites (not on --release-version-from-package, which the hand-rolled call may omit in favour of --version) or it will not catch the drift."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-26T18:42:06.810Z"}],"before_hash":"259f6eb50fbf1bdc30872f1521d7c8567e31bb962113a4735679e5a39d45a442","after_hash":"e223a62289c45959f4286e33963fc52eddd767a7bd184eaf68f41989bce763be","item_hash_version":2}
